# WHYspace Workspace Navigation

## Spatial Canvas

The WHYspace desktop is a **zero-gravity spatial canvas** — windows float in 2D space without a rigid grid. This creates a feel similar to VisionOS, combined with the productivity of a traditional desktop.

### Interaction Model

| Action | Input | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| Move window | Drag title bar | Free float, snaps to screen edge |
| Resize window | Drag corner/border | Maintains aspect ratio (optional) |
| Focus window | Click anywhere | Raises to top, routes keyboard |
| Close window | Click X | Saves state, terminates program |
| Minimize | Click — | Goes to taskbar, preserves state |
| Maximize | Double-click title | Full canvas, not fullscreen |

### Spatial Zones

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  TOP BAR                                             │
│  [Provider ◆ Gemini 2.0]  [● ONLINE]  [Mem: 42%]   │
├──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ LAUNCH   │  SPATIAL CANVAS (2048×1152 virtual)      │
│ PAD      │  ┌──────┐    ┌──────────────┐            │
│          │  │ Chat │    │  Code Studio │            │
│ ───────  │  │  📝  │    │   [FOCUSED]  │            │
│ ○ Chat   │  └──────┘    └──────────────┘            │
│ ○ Code   │         ┌──────────────────┐             │
│ ○ Mem    │         │  Memory Vault    │             │
│ ○ Res    │         │   (background)   │             │
│ ○ Img    │         └──────────────────┘             │
│ ○ Voice  │                                          │
│ ○ Wrkfl  │     ┌──────────────────────────┐         │
│ ○ Term   │     │  Research Agent          │         │
│          │     │  loading... ████████░░    │         │
│          │     └──────────────────────────┘         │
├──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  TASKBAR                                            │
│  ◆ Start  │ ✦ Chat │ ✦ Code St. │ ✦ Mem │ ✦ Res │ ⏰│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Window Manager

### Window State

```typescript
interface WindowState {
  id: string;           // unique window ID
  programId: string;    // refers to ProgramManifest.id
  title: string;
  position: { x: number; y: number };
  size: { width: number; height: number };
  minimized: boolean;
  focused: boolean;
  zIndex: number;
  state: 'loading' | 'ready' | 'error';
}
```

### Tiling Support

Windows can optionally snap to a tiling grid:

| Shortcut | Action |
|---|---|
| `Win+←` | Tile left half |
| `Win+→` | Tile right half |
| `Win+↑` | Tile top half |
| `Win+↓` | Tile bottom half |
| `Win+Shift+←` | Move to left monitor (future) |

